4. Design blog using bootstrap

    1. To install bootstrap in your application, run below command
        i. open new terminal
        ii. npm install bootstrap@4.6
            To install latest version use below commend
                npm i bootstrap@5.3.3 or npm i bootstrap@latest get it from https://getbootstrap.com/

    2. To use bootstrap method into our angular project there are three methods
        Note: Make sure to use only one from below in your project.
              It you are using one then remove changes related to other ways.

        i.  Add bootstrap css file to the angular using angular.json file
            open angular.json file
            Add bootstrap.min.css path within styles section
            "node_modules/bootstrap/dist/css/bootstrap.min.css"
            Restrart the app using ng serve

        ii. Add bootstrap css file to index.html like below
            <link rel="stylesheet" href="node_modules/bootstrap/dist/css/bootstrap.min.css">
          
        iii. Add bootstrap css file directly into styles.css
            @import '~bootstrap/dist/css/bootstrap.min.css'

5. create common css variable value
    Create them in styles.css
    We put those css variables inside below root
        :root{
            --primary-color:  #026467;
        }
    Like in typescript we use let or const to define a variabl, but here we use -- to define
    Get the color codes from https://www.figma.com/color-wheel/

6. We can define font in angular app like below
    copy the style url from below google font link as per the style we want and paste it into style.css
